Tensor.hpp and CreateRandomTensor.hpp included <omp.h> unconditionally without using it. The
Python bindings' code generator parses the headers without -fopenmp, and with GCC omp.h lives
in the compiler's builtin directory, which the generator does not search; on linux-64 the
pyeinsums build stopped at Tensor.hpp. Two tests and a benchmark that call omp_* functions now
include it themselves. Fixed in Einsums after 2.0.0a1.

